// lib/products-supplements.ts
// Supplements imported from The Feed's Supplements category (thefeed.com/supplements) on
// 2026-09-26, Phase 1: creatine, athlete performance (beta-alanine, bicarb, caffeine, nitric
// oxide, adaptogens, pre-workout, strength), recovery (tart cherry, collagen, joint support,
// beets, aminos, turmeric, injury), sleep, gut & biotics, and the athlete-relevant vitamins and
// minerals (iron, magnesium, zinc, vitamin D, omegas). Phase 2a (2026-09-28) added B and C
// vitamins, multivitamins, calcium, immune support, greens and reds drinks, fibre and prebiotics,
// colostrum and anti-inflammatories, energy, nootropics and ketones. Bundles, stacks, samples,
// children's products and products already in lib/products.ts were skipped; hormone, stress,
// liver and metabolic products are held for Phase 2b.
//
// Where the data comes from:
// - Ingredient amounts, the ingredient list, serving size, certifications, diet flags and prices
//   are taken from each product's page on The Feed. Price is the pack closest to a standard size;
//   servingsPerContainer is that pack's serving count (left out when the page doesn't give one).
// - NSF Certified for Sport was then checked against NSF's own database on 2026-10-05 (see
//   lib/certification-checks.ts): listings NSF didn't have were removed, and NSF-certified
//   products The Feed didn't flag were added.
// - rating / reviewCount are The Feed's own customer ratings, credited as "The Feed"; products
//   without ratings there show "No reviews yet".
// - sentiment is left empty: there's no per-attribute data to use.
// - Ingredient verdicts and notes are Pello's own summaries of the research on each ingredient,
//   never claims about the product.
// - transparencyScore uses the same formula as lib/products-thefeed.ts: full ingredient list 35 +
//   supplement facts with amounts 25 + no proprietary blend 15 + caffeine clear 10 + third-party
//   tested 15. null = not yet scored, because the page doesn't give the full label.

